course: dictionary
lesson: 3449
title: Facts and opinions
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fact is something known to be true, and you can check it. «A week is 7 days» is a fact. You can count the days to prove it.
explain: An opinion is what someone thinks or feels. «Dogs are the best pets» is an opinion, because someone else might think cats are better. Ask yourself: can I check this, or does it depend on who is speaking?
explain: The word fact also has a phrase, «in fact», which means really or actually. «In fact they all join into one world ocean» tells you the oceans are not separate, they really are one ocean.
fact: A fact is something that is known to be true and can be checked.
fact: «A week is 7 days» is a fact.
fact: Facts are different from opinions, which are what someone thinks or feels.
fact: «In fact» means really or actually.
fact: «Maths facts» are basic sums and times tables, like 6 × 7 = 42.
exercise: «A year has 12 months.» Is this a fact or an opinion? | An opinion | A question | A feeling | *A fact
exercise: Which sentence is an opinion? | A week is 7 days | Ten is more than seven | *Pizza is the tastiest food | There are 60 minutes in an hour
exercise: «In fact they all join into one world ocean.» What does in fact mean here? | Not at all | Without any water | *Really or actually | Quickly
test: In a non-fiction book, what is the index? | *The list of topics at the back, with page numbers | The list of all the library's books | A story told in the middle of the book | The picture on the front cover
test: Which of these is a fact you can check? | Dogs are the best pets | Reading is boring | *Ten is more than seven | Cats are nicer than dogs
exam: Sam says, «Dogs are the best pets.» Is this a fact or an opinion, and why? | A fact, because Sam said it | A fact, because it is written down in a book | An opinion, because it has the word dogs in it | *An opinion, because it is what Sam thinks and cannot be proved as true
